INT. SUNKEN CATHEDRAL OF THE DRAGON-KINGS - NIGHT

A vaulted nave drowned to the knees in black water. Columns of fossil bone rise into shadow. Crystal lanterns drift in the air, spilling cold green light on scales as large as shields, set into the floor like tiles of an immense mosaic.

TAMSIN BRIGHTWELL (30s, mercenary, chainmail and a ragged scarlet cloak, a notched longsword on her back) wades along the central aisle, torch sputtering. Behind her, UDO HARTSHORN (60s, a priest's grey robe hitched to his thighs, a holy book wrapped in oilcloth) clutches the hem of his habit above the waterline.

                    TAMSIN
          Stay close.

                    UDO
          I could hardly stray.

                    TAMSIN
          The last priest strayed.

                    UDO
          And?

                    TAMSIN
          We didn't find him.

Udo stops. Looks down. A scale shifts under the water, patient as a sleeping thing turning over.

                    UDO
          (to himself)
          Lord, steady these old knees.

Tamsin lifts the torch. At the aisle's end stands an altar, black basalt, its top a shallow bowl. In the bowl floats a single burning flame, small as a candle, steady in the still, cold air.

                    TAMSIN
          That's the Ember.

                    UDO
          It's smaller than the legends.

                    TAMSIN
          Everything is.

She advances. Udo follows. The water ripples. Not from them.

                    WARDEN (V.O.)
                (a voice like gravel in a bell)
          Who comes to the Hall of Ash?

Tamsin stops. Draws her sword in one smooth rasp. Udo clutches his book.

                    TAMSIN
          (to the nave)
          We seek the Ember.

                    WARDEN (V.O.)
          Many have sought it.

                    UDO
          (low, to Tamsin)
          Do not provoke it.

                    TAMSIN
          (low)
          I'm not provoking.

                    WARDEN (V.O.)
          You carry iron. You carry prayer. Which will you offer?

                    TAMSIN
          Neither.

                    UDO
          Tamsin.

                    TAMSIN
          I offer a trade.

Silence. The lanterns stop drifting.

                    WARDEN (V.O.)
          Speak.

                    TAMSIN
          My name for your fire. A true one. The first thing I was ever called.

Udo gasps. She doesn't look at him.

                    UDO
          Child, no. A name is a life.

                    TAMSIN
          It's a word.

                    WARDEN (V.O.)
          Words are life.

The water stills completely. A great shape moves under the floor of scales, a ripple traveling the length of the nave, until the whole cathedral seems to breathe in.

                    WARDEN (V.O.) (CONT'D)
          Accepted.

Tamsin lets her sword drop to her side. Opens her mouth. Whispers a single syllable that neither the audience nor Udo can hear.

The flame leaps from the bowl, a tongue of white fire twisting through the air, and settles in her open palm. It does not burn. It purrs.

Udo falls to his knees in the water, tears in his eyes. Tamsin stares at the flame, then at him.

                    TAMSIN (CONT'D)
          Say it back to me.

                    UDO
          I cannot.

                    TAMSIN
          Say what you heard.

                    UDO
          I heard nothing.

                    TAMSIN
          (softly)
          Good.

The Warden's laughter rolls across the vault, and the water rises.

                    UDO
          Run!

They run. Behind them the scales rise from the floor one by one, glittering, and the nave ceiling cracks.

                    TAMSIN
          (shouting over the thunder, to no one)
          I'll miss it!

                    WARDEN (V.O.)
          You will not even remember.

The doors slam shut behind them. Silence. The torch hisses out, and in the new dark, a very faint voice, half sob, half laugh, whispers from the stairwell, "What was my name?"
